---
import { ArrowRight } from '@lucide/astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About Cozy Crochet Gifts" description="Learn what Cozy Crochet Gifts offers and the values behind its crochet pattern storefront.">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">A little about the shop</p>
      <h1>Made for the moments you make by hand.</h1>
      <p>Cozy Crochet Gifts is a home for downloadable crochet patterns, amigurumi ideas, and inspiration for handmade gifts.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <img class="about-image" src="/images/home-crochet-still-life-1200.jpg" alt="A crocheted bunny and blanket beside yarn in a calm, sunlit studio." width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our point of view</p>
        <h2>A good pattern should help you feel ready to begin.</h2>
        <p>The shop is designed for crochet makers who enjoy creating small characters, useful gifts, and comforting projects at their own pace. Pattern listings are built around clear project information, so makers can check the details before choosing what to make.</p>
        <p>Cozy Crochet Gifts offers digital crochet pattern files. Gumroad handles checkout and file delivery for listed products; no finished handmade item is shipped from the storefront.</p>
        <p>We value thoughtful design, transparent descriptions, and useful reading that respects the time and care a handmade project takes. The shop is shaped around patient making, thoughtful product details, and useful reading for people who enjoy creating by hand.</p>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/shop/">Explore the shop <ArrowRight size={16} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="section section-soft">
    <div class="page-shell intro-band">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">What you can expect</p><h2>Information first, then inspiration.</h2></div>
      <div class="intro-band-copy">
        <p>When a pattern is available, its listing will show the verified information supplied for that project, including the file format, skill level, materials, and included files where known.</p>
        <p>For project-specific terms, always read the pattern listing and license. Product pages should make the practical details easy to find before you visit Gumroad to check out.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/faq/">Visit the FAQ <ArrowRight size={15} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>